-- title:
--   Principal repartitions are the constant families
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra. A place of the pair, an element of `Place K F`, is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of every element of $K$, distinct from all of $F$, and a principal ideal ring; each such $v$ carries the valuation `adicValuation` with values in $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$ attached to its height-one spectrum point. The $F$-subalgebra `repartitions K F` of the function space $\mathrm{Place}\,K\,F \to F$ is the $F$-algebra generated by those families $\alpha$ for which $\{v : \neg\, v.\mathrm{adicValuation}(\alpha_v) \le 1\}$ is finite, and `principalRepartitions K F` is the $K$-submodule of it obtained by restricting scalars from the range of the $F$-linear structure map $F \to$ `repartitions K F`. On the ambient function space, `globalSub K F` is the $K$-submodule given by the range of `diagonalHom`, the $K$-linear map sending $f \in F$ to the constant family $v \mapsto f$. For an element $\alpha$ of the subalgebra `repartitions K F`, the theorem asserts the equivalence: $\alpha$ lies in `principalRepartitions K F` if and only if the underlying function $\mathrm{Place}\,K\,F \to F$ obtained from $\alpha$ lies in `globalSub K F`. There are no further hypotheses.
--
--   This identifies the principal repartitions in the sense of Weil's repartition (Chevalley adèle) formalism with the principal, i.e. constant, adèles of the adelic model, so that the two descriptions of the diagonal copy of $F$ agree; it is the bridge used in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_linearEquiv_adeleSpaceQuot_H1`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_linearEquiv_adeleSpaceQuot_H1), which compares the adèle-space quotient with $H^1$ of a divisor.
